+# Validation status — AAIAP v0.1.1-demo
+
+**NOT YET VALIDATED AGAINST A GROUND STATION.**
+
+The daily NASA POWER meteorological data are gridded / model-based; they are not measurements at a Nebraska research plot. No verified ground-station comparisons for the published coordinates have been collected in this offline build environment. Consequently there are **no claimed bias, MAE, RMSE or correlation values**.
+
+## Reproduction plan
+1. Obtain daily NASA POWER point data for 2025 at the site reference coordinates.
+2. Obtain Nebraska Mesonet or NOAA station observations at a documented, nearby station under the provider's licence, with site ID and coordinates.
+3. Harmonise units, timezone, local solar day and missing value conventions.
+4. Align overlapping daily dates (do not fill missing days); aggregate monthly values only when coverage is adequate.
+5. Compute bias (POWER - station), MAE and RMSE for temperature and precipitation separately, and report sample count and time coverage.
+6. Publish the station name, source URL, access date, findings and caveats.
+
+The attached `scripts/validate_power.py` accepts **two reviewed CSV files** and computes metrics; it does not fabricate station readings.
